      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "\n\n```html\n<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n  <head>\n    <style>\n      #my-span {\n        color: black;\n      }\n    </style>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <span id=\"my-span\">Hover over me!</span>\n\n    <script>\n      const span = document.getElementById(\"my-span\");\n\n      span.addEventListener(\"mouseover\", function () {\n        this.style.color = \"red\";\n      });\n\n      span.addEventListener(\"mouseout\", function () {\n        this.style.color = \"black\"; // revert color on mouse out\n      });\n    </script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n```\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfc6 Which method should you use?\n\n| Method | Best For |\n|---|---|\n| **CSS `:hover`** | Simple, clean styling \u2014 always preferred |\n| **Inline JS** | Quick tests or very simple cases |\n| **External JS** | Dynamic or complex color-change logic |\n\nThe **CSS `:hover` method** is almost always the best choice as it keeps your styling clean, separated, and easy to maintain.",
